Yes, the image is highly relevant to the research matter of the attached PDFs, particularly the 2017 *npj Vaccines* paper. The PDFs investigate Nano-11's *in vivo* behavior as a vaccine adjuvant, including its transport to draining lymph nodes and targeting of antigen-presenting cells (APCs). The image directly supports these aspects by showing the presence and distribution of Nano-11 in different myeloid cell subsets (MigDC, LTDC, Mo/MΦ) within the draining lymph nodes over time, and quantifying Nano-11 uptake by these cells (MFI). This visual evidence substantiates the papers' claims about Nano-11's mechanism of action in activating adaptive immunity.